WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.304 --> 00:00:14.754
Tina: I can't believe how far away the door seems.

2
00:00:14.794 --> 00:00:18.076
Danny: I'm tired of being tiny.

3
00:00:18.817 --> 00:00:19.938
I wish I were big.

4
00:00:19.958 --> 00:00:21.359
Bello: Me too.

5
00:00:21.399 --> 00:00:24.542
Chuck: You, me, and all of us!

6
00:00:28.885 --> 00:00:31.888
Bello: How are we going to get in?

7
00:00:32.556 --> 00:00:34.117
Dave: There's no way we can lift it.

8
00:00:34.137 --> 00:00:36.960
Brad: Don't worry, we don't have to lift it.

9
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.461
Dave: What do you mean?

10
00:00:38.481 --> 00:00:42.444
Brad: My dad always complains that it doesn't close right.

11
00:00:42.464 --> 00:00:45.566
Brad: There has to be a small gap somewhere.

12
00:00:45.586 --> 00:00:50.090
Danny: Well, I don't see any gap here.

13
00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:52.072
Tina: Let's try over there.

14
00:00:55.875 --> 00:00:56.895
There it is up ahead.

15
00:00:56.915 --> 00:00:58.577
Brad: I told you.

16
00:00:58.597 --> 00:00:59.958
Danny: Come on!

17
00:00:59.978 --> 00:01:02.280
Bello: Quick, let's get inside.

18
00:01:06.254 --> 00:01:15.741
Mrs. Rice: How did that sheet fly over my head?

19
00:01:15.761 --> 00:01:18.743
Mrs. Rice: It couldn't have been Tina or the giant.

20
00:01:18.763 --> 00:01:20.565
Mrs. Rice: I would have seen them.

21
00:01:22.986 --> 00:01:25.348
It must have been an invisible giant!

22
00:01:25.368 --> 00:01:27.570
Mrs. Rice: And it must be nearby!

23
00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:30.172
I have to warn someone.

24
00:01:39.272 --> 00:01:41.813
Bello: I can't believe how huge everything looks.

25
00:01:42.594 --> 00:01:44.235
It seemed so small before.

26
00:01:44.255 --> 00:01:48.297
Chuck: Danny, how are we going to be able to do anything here?

27
00:01:48.317 --> 00:01:50.078
Chuck: We're too tiny.

28
00:01:50.098 --> 00:01:52.960
Danny: We have our imaginations.

29
00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:54.321
Trust me.

30
00:01:54.341 --> 00:01:58.223
Danny: If we use our imaginations, we can do anything.

31
00:01:58.243 --> 00:02:02.325
Brad: First, we have to get the nano-putty.

32
00:02:02.345 --> 00:02:04.046
Dave: Where is it?

33
00:02:04.066 --> 00:02:06.708
Brad: It's in that filing cabinet.

34
00:02:07.992 --> 00:02:09.053
Tina: All right, everybody.

35
00:02:09.393 --> 00:02:10.014
Let's go.

36
00:02:10.034 --> 00:02:17.040
Chuck: Where did you get this magic putty from in the first place?

37
00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:20.042
Brad: My dad is a top secret scientist.

38
00:02:20.663 --> 00:02:24.066
Brad: I found the nano-putty one day when I was playing in the garage.

39
00:02:24.086 --> 00:02:26.828
Brad: I think my dad brought it home from his lab.

40
00:02:26.848 --> 00:02:29.170
Dave: Wow, that's pretty cool.

41
00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:31.952
Brad: We're almost there.

42
00:02:31.972 --> 00:02:36.116
Brad: The nano-putty is in the bottom drawer of the filing cabinet.

43
00:02:44.416 --> 00:02:44.996
Tina: What was that?

44
00:02:45.016 --> 00:02:47.797
Danny: A lightbulb just exploded!

45
00:02:47.817 --> 00:02:52.119
Chuck: We're under attack!

46
00:02:52.659 --> 00:02:53.660
Bello: Hurry, everybody!

47
00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:55.941
Tina: Watch out!

48
00:02:55.961 --> 00:03:03.764
Tina: Who could be attacking us?

49
00:03:03.784 --> 00:03:05.985
Chuck: It came from up there.

50
00:03:06.005 --> 00:03:10.587
Danny: It's just Brad's cat.

51
00:03:11.247 --> 00:03:13.268
It must have knocked some things off the table.

52
00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:15.403
Brad: She didn't mean to hurt us.

53
00:03:16.025 --> 00:03:17.027
She's a good kitty.
